{
  "subject": {
    "slug": "treatment-planning",
    "title": "Treatment Planning",
    "order": 13
  },
  "lesson": {
    "slug": "treatment-planning-breast",
    "title": "Breast Treatment Planning",
    "order": 0,
    "pages": [
      {
        "title": "Three Fractionation Approaches",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Breast radiation therapy uses several distinct fractionation schedules, each with real tradeoffs:"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Schedule"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Typical Regimen"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Conventional (CFRT)",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "50 Gy in 25 fractions (2 Gy/fx)"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Hypofractionation (HFRT)",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "40 Gy in 15 fractions (2.67 Gy/fx)"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Accelerated Partial Breast Irradiation (APBI)",
                                  "marks": [
                                    {
                                      "type": "bold"
                                    }
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "~30 Gy in 5 fractions (6 Gy/fx)"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "callout",
                  "attrs": {
                    "kind": "key-principle"
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "APBI's much larger fraction size demands ultra-precise delivery techniques (VMAT/SBRT-style precision) to avoid toxic hot spots while still meeting OAR constraints \u2014 the margin for error shrinks considerably compared to conventional fractionation."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Delivery Techniques",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "3D-CRT (conventional tangents)",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " uses simple opposed beams \u2014 straightforward, but with poorer dose homogeneity and higher heart/lung dose for left-sided tumors specifically."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "VMAT/IMRT",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " uses continuous or multiple shaped fields to improve homogeneity and actively sculpt dose around OARs \u2014 especially valuable for hypofractionated and APBI schedules, where precision matters most."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Deep Inspiration Breath Hold (DIBH)",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "DIBH",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "bold"
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": " is used specifically for left-sided breast treatment \u2014 the patient holds a deep breath, which physically pushes the heart away from the chest wall, drastically reducing mean heart dose during treatment."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "lq_page3_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "DIBH is most relevant for which patients?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "Right-sided breast cancer patients",
              "Left-sided breast cancer patients"
            ],
            "answer": 1,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "DIBH specifically addresses the heart's proximity to left-sided treatment fields \u2014 right-sided fields don't have the same heart-dose concern."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "OAR Constraints",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Structure"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Constraint"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ],
                          "attrs": {
                            "header": true
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Heart (left-sided treatment)"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Mean dose \u2264 4 Gy (goal < 1 Gy with DIBH)"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Ipsilateral lung"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "V20 \u2264 10% (whole breast treatment)"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "tableRow",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Contralateral breast"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "type": "tableCell",
                          "content": [
                            {
                              "type": "paragraph",
                              "content": [
                                {
                                  "type": "text",
                                  "text": "Mean dose \u2264 1 Gy"
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Note that the biological effect (EQD2) of a given physical dose depends heavily on the fractionation schedule \u2014 a constraint expressed in physical Gy means something different under conventional vs. hypofractionated vs. APBI schedules."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "knowledge_check",
            "key": "lq_page4_1",
            "stem": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "What is the goal mean heart dose for a left-sided breast treatment using DIBH?"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            "options": [
              "Less than 1 Gy",
              "Less than 10 Gy"
            ],
            "answer": 0,
            "explanation": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "With DIBH actively pulling the heart away from the field, the goal mean heart dose drops to under 1 Gy, well below the 4 Gy constraint without DIBH."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Putting It Together \u2014 A Planning Decision",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Consider a left-sided patient being planned for whole-breast conventional fractionation. The plan will likely use tangent fields (3D-CRT or VMAT), and DIBH should be strongly considered specifically because of the left-sided heart proximity \u2014 this is exactly the kind of technique-selection decision that shows up constantly in real planning."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "For a patient being considered for APBI instead, the tighter fractionation (5 fractions, larger dose per fraction) raises the bar on setup precision and technique selection well above what conventional whole-breast treatment requires."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Ready for Hands-On Practice",
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "rich_text",
            "body": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "You've covered the three fractionation approaches, delivery technique tradeoffs, DIBH, and the specific OAR dose constraints for breast treatment."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The Treatment Planning Suite has a Breast \u2014 Left Chest Wall dataset preloaded with a PTV and nearby OARs (heart, ipsilateral lung) already seeded \u2014 a left-sided case, deliberately, so you can practice exactly the heart-sparing planning tradeoffs covered in this lesson."
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
